  "steps": [
    "Brown the beef. Heat a large skillet over medium heat. Add the beef and onion; season with salt, pepper, chili powder, cumin, garlic powder and dried cilantro.",
    "Add the pasta. Once the beef is cooked through, drain excess grease, then add garlic, macaroni, broth, Rotel and tomato sauce. Stir well and bring to a quick boil.",
    "Simmer. Turn down to medium-low, cover and cook about 12 minutes until the pasta is done, stirring once halfway.",
    "Finish. Stir in the cheese and milk and let sit until melted. Top with fresh cilantro."
